From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:24:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: rkvdec: vdpu383: Complete the request when rejecting a
 HEVC job

When the SPS RPS controls are missing, rkvdec_hevc_run() returns -EINVAL
after rkvdec_hevc_run_preamble() has applied the request's controls,
but without calling rkvdec_run_postamble(). The buffers are then
returned with VB2_BUF_STATE_ERROR, but the control handler object of
the request is never completed, so the request never reaches the
complete state and userspace waiting on the request fd waits forever.

Call rkvdec_run_postamble() before returning the error.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu383-hevc.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu383-hevc.c b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu383-hevc.c
index a672fa894..ef4ce05f1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu383-hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/rockchip/rkvdec/rkvdec-vdpu383-hevc.c
@@ -553,6 +553,8 @@ static int rkvdec_hevc_run(struct rkvdec_ctx *ctx)
 	if ((run.sps->num_long_term_ref_pics_sps && !run.ext_sps_lt_rps) ||
 	    (run.sps->num_short_term_ref_pic_sets && !run.ext_sps_st_rps)) {
 		dev_err_ratelimited(core->dev, "Long and short term RPS not set\n");
+		/* Complete the request's controls, or the request never completes. */
+		rkvdec_run_postamble(ctx, &run.base);
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
